      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "VIRGILIA.\nI thank your Ladyship; well, good madam.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28311/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28311/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 50,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 848023,
        "end": 848103,
        "line": 31939,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap06/p@28311",
        "anchor": "sceneI_6.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "VIRGILIA.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28395",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "VOLUMNIA.\nHe had rather see the swords and hear a drum than look upon his schoolmaster.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28395/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28395/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 87,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 848107,
        "end": 848224,
        "line": 31944,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap06/p@28395",
        "anchor": "sceneI_6.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "VOLUMNIA.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28516",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "VALERIA.\nO’ my word, the father’s son! I’ll swear ’tis a very pretty boy. O’ my troth, I looked upon him o’ Wednesday half an hour together. H’as such a confirmed countenance. I saw him run after a gilded butterfly, and when he caught it, he let it go again, and after it again, and over and over he comes, and up again, catched it again. Or whether his fall enraged him or how ’twas, he did so set his teeth and tear it. O, I warrant how he mammocked it!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28516/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@28516/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 455,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 848228,
        "end": 848718,
        "line": 31949,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap06/p@28516",
        "anchor": "sceneI_6.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "VALERIA.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@29010",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "VOLUMNIA.\nOne on’s father’s moods.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@29010/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneI_6.3/p@29010/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 34,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
